EXT. SCHOOL QUAD - DAY

Autumn. A bench under a bare tree, covered in flowers and candles. Students drift past. NOOR (17) stands apart, arms folded.

JESS (17) joins her, holding a candle she has not lit.

JESS
Since Sam's suicide they are saying it was a beautiful sacrifice. Like he did it for us.

NOOR
He did not do anything for us.

INT. NOOR'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

Noor lies on the bed with headphones in. On the laptop, a memorial video for Sam, who died by suicide last month, plays: photographs, slow music, the words HE CHOSE PEACE in white type.

A text from Jess: "same time next year. every year. for him."

Noor closes the laptop.

INT. NOOR'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

Noor's mother, RANIA (40s), is at the sink. She sees the self-harm marks on Noor's forearm as Noor reaches for a glass. She does not gasp. She turns off the tap.

RANIA
Can I sit with you a minute?

Noor shrugs. Rania sits.

RANIA (CONT'D)
I noticed your arm. You do not have to explain it tonight. I want to know what would help, and I want us to talk to someone who knows more than I do. Together.

NOOR
(barely)
Okay.

EXT. SCHOOL QUAD - DAY (ONE YEAR LATER)

The bench again. More candles. A banner reads HE CHOSE PEACE. Jess lights the candle she kept for the anniversary of the suicide.

JESS
Same time next year.

INT. NOOR'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

Noor does not open the laptop. She opens a notebook instead and writes a name, then a phone number, then underlines it twice.

EXT. SCHOOL QUAD - DUSK

Noor sits on the bench alone. She takes the banner down, folds it, and puts it under her arm. She walks toward the gate, where Rania is waiting with the car running.

FADE OUT.
